# Phone / PWA

**Chat name:** `Phone`  
**Sidebar label:** n/a  
**Agent starter:** `.cursor/agents/phone.md`

## Phone bottom bar

Phone only (`md:hidden`). Desktop/iPad keep the sidebar.

| Slot | Tabs |
|------|------|
| Bottom bar | Pipeline · Calendar · Tasks · Tools · Profile |
| Swipe up (More) | Documents |

Logo in the header goes Home. No Home tab. Profile opens `settings`. On Home, no tab is selected.

Phone header has no avatar menu. Install app and Sign out live at the bottom of Profile settings.

Handle on the tab bar opens the More sheet (same as swipe up). Swipe down or tap the dimmer to close. Tapping Documents keeps Documents **inside that sheet** (full-height is OK) — it must not call `openNavTab('documents')` on phone and replace the app. Swipe down returns to the tab they were on. iPad: no More sheet; Documents stays in the sidebar.

Finger pagers (iPhone **and** iPad): gate on `TouchEvent` / `pointerType === 'touch'`, **not** `max-width: 767px`. Mouse / trackpad / keyboard case: click and kanban drag only — no pagers. iPad keeps the sidebar; do not put the phone tab bar on iPad.

Full-width swipe (edges **and** center, including bezels): finger right = previous, finger left = next. Horizontal page swipe wins on form fields and chip rows unless the finger is clearly scrolling vertically or pinching. Pinch-zoom stays on. Maps keep a leftover edge yield so pan/pin-drag still work — do not turn the whole map into a pager.

Inside a lead this is a **linear chip pager** (Overview → Pipeline → Measurements → Financial → Insurance → Messages → Estimates → Orders → Photos → Documents) — not visit history. Tapping a chip and swiping to that chip are the same place. Body **and** chip-row swipe walk that order. On Overview, one more previous-swipe leaves the job (silent save) to the Pipeline board (All). Last chip (Documents) rubber-bands.

Pipeline jump chips: All → Lead → Prospect → Approved → Completed → Invoiced → Closed. Swipe = tap. On All, one more previous-swipe is Home. Next-swipe from Home does nothing. Pipeline list cards are tap-to-open only (no swipe-to-stage). Job stage inside a lead is tap only. Bottom tabs are tap only. Maps keep a small edge yield so pan/pin-drag still work.

Pull-to-refresh (finger, scroll top): Home, Pipeline, Tasks, Calendar, Weather, lead Documents, lead Photos. Not Documents hub, lead Messages, or forms. Spinner lives in the pull gap under the header. Skip pull when the touch starts on `.weather-map` / `.leaflet-container`.

`phoneTabBar` / `phoneTabSheet` in `app/page.tsx` (`renderPhoneTabBar`).

